# Install devDependencies even when NODE_ENV=production.
#
# The API must run with NODE_ENV=production — that is what puts the refresh cookie into
# `SameSite=None; Secure`, without which cross-site auth between the Vercel frontend and this API
# silently fails on every token refresh.
#
# npm reads the same variable during install and omits devDependencies when it is `production`.
# TypeScript and every `@types/*` package live there, so the install succeeds and the build then
# fails with 99 errors, opening with:
#
#   TS7016: Could not find a declaration file for module 'express'
#
# which reads as a missing dependency rather than what it is — a deliberately skipped one. The
# advice the compiler prints ("npm i --save-dev @types/express") does not help: it is already in
# package.json and already in the lockfile.
#
# This lives in `.npmrc` rather than only in the build command because the build command is a
# *platform setting*. Render stores it on the service when the Blueprint is first applied and does
# not re-read `render.yaml` on a plain push, so fixing the command in that file left the deploy
# still running the old one. A committed `.npmrc` cannot drift from the repository, and it fixes
# the build on any host that installs with NODE_ENV=production — Render, Docker, CI.
#
# The runtime is unaffected: the start command runs compiled JavaScript and needs nothing from
# devDependencies.
include=dev
